Feedback for First Sprint


1. Aesthetics – How does it look?
Contrast – Text is clear and easy to read.
Alignment – Everything is lined up neatly.
Proximity – Related items are close; unrelated items have space.
Consistency – Same fonts, colours, and styles across pages.
Balance – Not too crowded or too empty.
White Space – Enough empty space around text and images.
Score (0–6): 6
Feedback:
I love the colours used for the website - the use of them made it clear where things started and stopped. The headings were very clear which made it easy to find the information needed for knowing what each thing was about. You could use a different font.

2. Functionality – Does it work?
Links – All links work and go to the right place.
Navigation – Menus and buttons take you where expected.
Scrolling – You can scroll without problems.
Page Load – No errors; all images and text appear.
Responsive – Works well on a desktop screen.
Score (0–5): 5
Feedback:
The website was very easy to navigate and use. The videos worked perfectly and it was clear what needed to be pressed for things to work.

3. Usability – Is it easy to use?
Readability – Text is big enough and easy to read.
Accessibility – Clear headings, alt text for images, good contrast.
Find Info – Information is easy to find.
User Friendly – Feels welcoming and clear.
Score (0–4): 4
Feedback:
The website met all criteria above. You could put in text for the videos but that is probably not necessary.

4. Bonus Criteria (Optional)
Purpose – Easy to see what the site is about.
Engaging – Makes you want to explore more.
Spelling – No big spelling or grammar mistakes.
Score (0–3): 3
Feedback:
It was easy to see what the site was about due to the large headings. I like the use of Japanese but you could explain the meaning of the word.

Overall, the website was well laid out and easy to use. Improvements could be made on font variety and colours for headings. I also think you could explain the meaning of shizuka. The main heading is really cool, I like how you have used a real life painting for the background. The videos worked first-time and it was clear what they were for. It looks like an amazing website! 
- Ana


